      "description": "Watch Sheffield Wednesday vs Wolves highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 25, 2026. The lights of Hillsborough shone brightly on August 25, 2026, as Sheffield Wednesday hosted Premier League outfit Wolverhampton Wanderers in a high-stakes Carabao Cup tie. Both sides approached the fixture with intent, knowing that a place in the next round of the competition was the ultimate prize. Early Misfortune and Wednesday's Response The contest began in nightmare fashion for the home side. Within just three minutes, a cross into the box led to an unfortunate own goal by Sil Swinkels , gifting Wolverhampton Wanderers an immediate lead. The early setback forced the Owls to chase the game from the outset, while the visitors looked to capitalize on the momentum through the creative play of Tawanda Chirewa and the movement of Adam Armstrong . Despite the early blow, Sheffield Wednesday showed plenty of spirit. Kieran Morrison was a constant threat from distance, forcing José Sá into two crucial saves to keep the Wolves' lead intact. Mason Burstow also came agonizingly close to an equalizer, seeing his header from a corner fly just wide of the post. The Owls dominated a significant portion of the first half's possession, but clinical finishing remained elusive. Olagunju Doubles the Advantage As the first half entered stoppage time, Wolves delivered a clinical blow that changed the complexion of the match. A well-delivered corner from Tommy Doyle found Saheed Olagunju unmarked in the center of the penalty area. The young defender made no mistake, powering a header into the center of the goal to make it 2-0. It was a crushing moment for the hosts, who had fought valiantly to get back into the game only to concede a second just before the whistle. Second Half Management and Injuries The second period saw a tactical battle as both managers utilized their benches. Sheffield Wednesday introduced the experienced Barry Bannan and the pacey Louie Barry to ignite a comeback. While they managed to create several openings—most notably a late effort from Jamal Lowe —the Wolves defense held firm. The visitors managed the closing stages professionally, though the match was marred by late injuries to Wednesday's Harry Gray and Wolves' goalscorer Saheed Olagunju . In the end, the Premier League side's first-half efficiency proved to be the difference. Despite a spirited performance from the Championship side, Wolverhampton Wanderers secured their 2-0 victory and a spot in the next round, leaving Sheffield Wednesday to focus on their league campaign after a tough night at home."
